# Runtime Tools

Router rule. Triggers point at the reference material for the tool in
question — the Node note is in the `fnm` section below, the container notes
are in the `container-tools` skill.

## Load the relevant reference when any of these is true

- About to run any `node`, `npm`, `pnpm`, `yarn`, `npx`, `corepack`, or
  `bun` command in a project that has a `.node-version`, `.nvmrc`, or
  `package.json#engines.node` → read the `fnm` section below.
- About to run any `docker`, `podman`, `nerdctl`, or `containerd` command
  → load the `container-tools` skill.
- Editing or authoring a `Dockerfile`, `Containerfile`, `compose.yaml`,
  `compose.yml`, `docker-compose.yml`, or `podman-compose.yml` → load
  the `container-tools` skill.
- The user asks which Node version is active, or to install / switch
  Node → read the `fnm` section below.
- The user asks which container tool to use on this machine → load the
  `container-tools` skill.

